From 7e9162eb0f22dd29210f07a02648b0c6b78c9988 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jmgasper <jmgasper@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 03:32:47 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] zink/hgl: say what the present counter is for

It is not bookkeeping anybody needs; it is the thing that showed frames
stop when the window system says stop, which is how the staircase left
by a dragged window was traced to the repaint rather than to ordering.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/targets/haiku-zink/ZinkRenderer.h | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/targets/haiku-zink/ZinkRenderer.h b/src/gallium/targets/haiku-zink/ZinkRenderer.h
index bc946ca..2fdd658 100644
--- a/src/gallium/targets/haiku-zink/ZinkRenderer.h
+++ b/src/gallium/targets/haiku-zink/ZinkRenderer.h
@@ -58,6 +58,10 @@ private:
 			bool				fPresentedIntoScanout;
 			// whether ScanoutTarget took fInfoLocker and still holds it
 			bool				fScanoutTargetHeld;
+			// how many frames went into the screen since the window system
+			// last said anything, reported under ZINK_SCANOUT_TRACE. It is
+			// what shows whether a frame can be drawn at a place the window
+			// has already left.
 			int32				fPresentCount = 0;
 			// when the window last moved or its clipping changed
 			bigtime_t			fLastPlacementChange = 0;
